# Nexus Architecture (mandatory)

Source of truth: [`docs/architecture-blueprint.md`](docs/architecture-blueprint.md)

Before creating or substantially changing backend domains in `Nexus.Api` (or `Refactor/Nexus.Api`), **read and obey that document**. Do not invent a competing layout.

## Non-negotiables

- Domain/bounded context is the structural root — never role-first trees (`Operator/Payments`).
- Layers: `Domain/` · `Application/` · `Infrastructure/` · `Presentation/` · `Composition/`
- Roles only in `Application/Ports/In`, `Application/UseCases`, `Application/Authorization`, `Presentation/Http`
- One use case = one input port + one handler (no giant `IAdministrator` / `IOperator` services)
- Handlers return `IOperationResult<T>`; `*Result` is the success payload, not a second Result framework
- Controllers do not mutate aggregates; HTTP contracts stay in `Presentation`
- Aggregates own invariants; no persistence/transport details in Domain
- Event sourcing is a plug-in behind `I<Aggregate>Repository` — never expose `IEventStore` to use cases by default
- No role-specific aggregates for the same concept; no empty optional folders; no cross-domain `Infrastructure` references
- Domain events ≠ integration events; do not publish raw domain events as cross-context contracts

## Defaults

- Scaffold **minimum viable domain** only; add optional folders when needed
- Start state-based; add ES/projections later without changing application ports
- Group authorization policies by role/domain; split per capability only when justified
- Existing code outside this standard is debt — migrate opportunistically; do not copy it as the model

Deviations need an explicit reason in the change.
